runbooks/RUNNING_THE_LOOP.md:102:**Gating reviewer down.** A gating reviewer blocked by credit balance, quota, 429, expired-token, invalid-token, or the same provider/account failure as any other seat gets the provider-side failure treatment before the gate moves: keep the probe cadence by running `bun seats/adapter.ts probe <seat>` at about two, five, and ten minutes after the failure, and run it again on every commander tick while the review remains blocked. A `verify.ts` timeout is different: it is not a provider failure, must not start the probe cadence, and should be rerun with a per-repo budget (`bun seats/verify.ts ... --timeout-ms <ms>`) or the fleet override `WHEELHOUSE_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_MS=<ms>` after reading `seats/verdicts/<bead-id>.partial.md` for the last tool/phase and partial output. Do not park the bead merely because the first probe failed. If the probes keep failing and review is the only blocked stage, the commander may promote a FALLBACK GATE for that outage window, but only on the bead and only under all of these conditions: the fallback account is distinct from every author of the diff under review (the seat-accounting rule in `wheelhouse/fleet/SEATS.md`, and the on-disk same-directory STOP in `seats/verify.ts`, are the precedent); the fallback reviewer carries the full `wheelhouse/crew/REVIEWER.md` contract (own re-runs, evidence copied where the graph can reach it, verdict as a bead comment, and both `VERDICT:` and `PUSH:` lines); and the verdict line or its lead-in states that it is gating as fallback, names the outage, and names the distinct-account basis. This is per-outage promotion, not a roster change. A standing shadow seat is still only a mirror by default: shadow-never-gates-by-default means its verdict never gates a merge unless the commander promotes that seat for this specific outage on the bead, and even then the comment must stop being a shadow verdict and satisfy the fallback-gate sentence above.
seats/README.md:312:The default one-shot verifier budget is 900000 ms (15 minutes). Override it for one invocation/repository with `--timeout-ms <ms>` when a repository is known to have a long cold build, or set `WHEELHOUSE_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_MS=<ms>` in the environment; the environment wins over the flag so commander wrappers can impose a fleet-local ceiling. On timeout, `verify.ts` writes `seats/verdicts/<bead-id>.partial.md`, prints elapsed time and the last tool/phase it saw, and exits 1. A timeout is not a provider/auth failure and does not start the probe cadence.
